# .trivyignore — accepted-risk waivers for container scans.
#
# Every entry carries an `exp:` expiry; when a waiver lapses, the finding
# becomes a gate failure again and must be re-evaluated (bump the carrying
# dependency, or renew with justification). Waivers apply to the publish-time
# Trivy gates (publish-dashboard-images.yml) and the weekly audit
# (container-audit.yml). Each finding below was enumerated from a scan of the
# published digest ghcr.io/vibebb/dashboard-tools@sha256:792834c6... on
# 2026-10-03; see docs/operations.md "Container hardening" for the full
# analysis.
#
# --- npm-bundled node_modules in base images (dashboard-tools) --------------
# Vendored npm trees upstream ships inside the image: emsdk's own
# node 24.19.0 (emsdk/node/24.19.0_64bit/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules,
# where tar 7.5.16 is the CRITICAL), emsdk's upstream/emscripten/node_modules
# eslint/tooling deps (used by emcc at runtime — cannot be stripped), and
# the Node 26 install's bundled npm (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/
# node_modules — identical tree from the verified upstream tarball).
# brace-expansion, browserslist, fast-uri, flatted,
# ip-address, js-yaml, nanoid, picomatch, postcss, tar, undici. No upstream
# release with patched bundles exists yet; re-evaluate at the next
# emsdk release or NODE_VERSION bump — tracked in
# scripts/dependency_update_deferrals.json.
